# *.3md is Markdown extended along a Z axis (frontmatter + prose +
# @plane markers) — but GitHub's Linguist detects it as Roff, since a
# dot immediately followed by a digit (".3md") collides with Unix man-
# page section-number conventions (.1-.9, .3x, .3pm, ...), which is
# exactly what Roff's own file extensions look like. Confirmed this
# isn't a fluke: even CorvidLabs/agent-3md itself (the format's own
# origin repo) has the identical misdetection, unfixed.
#
# Tried `linguist-language=Markdown` first — fixed the language-stats
# bar, but real evidence (a human looking at the actual rendered page)
# showed it also makes GitHub's file view default to a "Preview" tab
# that renders the body as one collapsed paragraph: `.3md` isn't a
# genuinely markdown-recognized extension, so whatever render path a
# language override routes it through isn't the same one real `.md`
# files get — headings and paragraph breaks don't survive. That broke
# actual human readability, which matters far more than the stats bar.
# `linguist-documentation` instead: removes `.3md` from the language
# stats (fixing the original cosmetic complaint) without claiming a
# language, which should leave the file view on plain Code (each line
# preserved as written) rather than a broken Preview.
*.3md linguist-documentation
